I. Overall Design & Development Strategy
Color Palette: This must be strictly maintained from the screenshots. The primary brand colors appear to be:

Primary: A deep, professional blue (#003366 or similar).

Secondary: A warm, energetic orange (#FF6600 or similar).

Neutral: White, light grays (#F8F9FA), and dark gray/black for text.

Typography: Use a clean, modern, and highly readable sans-serif font (e.g., Google Fonts: Inter, Poppins, or Open Sans).

Core Values (Eliability, Reliability): These should be subtly woven into the website's copy and design. For example, in the "About Us" section, a tagline could be "Built on Reliability and Proven Eliability" or use a value proposition like "Delivering Reliable, Expert Solutions."

The "Our Partners" Section: This will be a dedicated section on the homepage or a separate page where partner logos are displayed. The logos will be animated (e.g., a slow, continuous scroll/marquee or fade-in/up on scroll) and perfectly aligned horizontally.

Navigation & Services Dropdown: The primary navigation will include "Home," "Services," and "Contact." When a user hovers over "Services," a vertical dropdown menu will appear, listing all the core service categories. Each item will be a clickable link.

