III. Development & Implementation Notes
HTML Structure (index.html, services.html, about.html, contact.html, service-detail.html): Use a clean, semantic HTML5 structure. The service-detail.html page can be a template that populates content dynamically or be duplicated for each service.

CSS Styling (style.css):

Color Management: Use CSS variables (custom properties) to define the primary and secondary colors for easy maintenance.

Navigation: Implement a pure CSS dropdown menu for the "Services" tab.

Animations: Use CSS animations (@keyframes) for the partner logo scroll/marquee. Use JavaScript for scroll-triggered animations (fade-in, slide-up) for a modern feel.

Mobile Responsiveness: Use media queries to ensure the website looks flawless on all devices (desktop, tablet, and mobile). The navigation should collapse into a "hamburger" menu on smaller screens.

Alignment: Ensure the text in the "Our Services" section is perfectly aligned as requested.

JavaScript (script.js):

Navigation: Toggle the hamburger menu on mobile.

Service Dropdown: Enhance the user experience for the dropdown.

"Learn More" Button Logic: Handle the click event to navigate to the appropriate service detail page. For a static page, this is a simple link. For a dynamic page, pass a parameter in the URL (e.g., ?service=corporate-training) to load the correct content.

Scroll Animations: Implement Intersection Observer API for scroll-triggered animations.

Content Integration: Meticulously copy the detailed, suggested content for each service into its designated place within the service-detail.html structure. Structure the content with proper headings (<h3>, <h4>), paragraphs (<p>), and lists (<ul>, <ol>) for readability.

Images & Icons:

Use professional, high-quality stock photos that are relevant to consulting and business.

Use a consistent icon set (e.g., Font Awesome) for service icons, benefits, and social media.